# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Name | Provider | Recommended use | Unique benefits | Cost per execution (RUs) |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| Tensor-Network Error Mitigation<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/algorithmiq-tem)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/cbvfdhv3i0vnwv4sxkdpp3pcvip27atd)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/algorithmiq-tem-eula.pdf)      | Algorithmiq  | Workloads that have low-weight observables and loop-free circuits. | Reduces measurement overhead and variance, outperforming standard error mitigation baselines such as Zero Noise Extrapolation (ZNE) and Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) for relevant circuit classes. | N/A |\n"
"| QESEM: Error Suppression and Error Mitigation<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/qedma-qesem)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/qedma-qesem/api-reference)    | Qedma        | Workloads that  include circuits with fractional or parameterized gates, high-weight observables,  and workflows that require unbiased expectation values and accurate runtime estimates. | Produces unbiased expectation values with lower variance and resource overhead, outperforming ZNE and PEC for relevant circuit classes. | N/A |\n"
"| Performance Management<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/q-ctrl-performance-management)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/q-ctrl-performance-management/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/ly9cs0lxy6nxqrirt5rt1xisnmvydj9z)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/q-ctrl-functions-eula.pdf) | Q-CTRL       | Workloads that contain parametric circuits, deep circuits, or require many circuit executions. | Automatically applies AI-driven error suppression to quantum algorithms, maximizing the performance of IBM devices to deliver accurate results while reducing the number of shots, compute time, and cost required. <br/><br/>Zero-overhead method that improves execution accuracy for the Sampler and the Estimator primitives, compatible with any weight of observables. | S: .5<br/> M: 1<br/>L: 5 |\n"
"| Orbit<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/quantum-elements-orbit)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/quantum-elements-orbit/api-reference) | Quantum Elements | Workloads containing idle periods or scheduling gaps, including static and dynamic circuits such as quantum error correction, mid-circuit measurement, oracular algorithms, variational quantum algorithms, and Hamiltonian simulation. | Combines optimized transpilation, dynamical decoupling, and measurement error mitigation into a unified workflow to improve circuit performance on IBM Quantum hardware. <br/><br/>Applies low-overhead error suppression that preserves the original circuit logic without additional quantum or classical pre-processing time, so that users can enable, disable, or compare each technique against the raw circuit. | S: 0<br/> M: 1<br/>L: 5 |\n"
"| AI-QEM<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/ltm-ai-qem)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/ltm-ai-qem/api-reference) | LTM | Estimator workloads, particularly utility-scale circuits with large depth and width, such as Hamiltonian simulation and mirror or Clifford benchmarking circuits. | Uses a graph convolutional network (GCN)-Transformer model, trained on circuit structure, backend topology, Pauli observables, and qubit calibrations, to predict a correction factor for each Pauli term. <br/><br/>Mitigates expectation values with no additional QPU time compared to the Estimator primitive, because the correction is applied during post-processing. | N/A |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Pangalan | Provider | Inirerekomendang paggamit | Natatanging benepisyo | Gastos kada execution (RUs) |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| Tensor-Network Error Mitigation<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/algorithmiq-tem)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/algorithmiq-tem/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/cbvfdhv3i0vnwv4sxkdpp3pcvip27atd)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/algorithmiq-tem-eula.pdf)      | Algorithmiq  | Mga workload na may low-weight observable at loop-free na circuit. | Binabawasan ang measurement overhead at variance, na mas mahusay kaysa sa standard na error mitigation baseline tulad ng Zero Noise Extrapolation (ZNE) at Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) para sa mga kaugnay na klase ng circuit. | N/A |\n"
"| QESEM: Error Suppression and Error Mitigation<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/qedma-qesem)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/qedma-qesem/api-reference)    | Qedma        | Mga workload na naglalaman ng mga circuit na may fractional o parameterized na gate, high-weight observable, at mga workflow na nangangailangan ng unbiased expectation values at tumpak na runtime estimate. | Nagpo-produce ng unbiased expectation values na may mas mababang variance at resource overhead, na mas mahusay kaysa sa ZNE at PEC para sa mga kaugnay na klase ng circuit. | N/A |\n"
"| Performance Management<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/q-ctrl-performance-management)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/q-ctrl-performance-management/api-reference)<br/>[License](https://ibm.box.com/s/ly9cs0lxy6nxqrirt5rt1xisnmvydj9z)<br/>[EULA](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/functions/eula/q-ctrl-functions-eula.pdf) | Q-CTRL       | Mga workload na may parametric circuit, malalim na circuit, o nangangailangan ng maraming circuit execution. | Awtomatikong naglalapat ng AI-driven error suppression sa mga quantum algorithm, na ini-maximize ang performance ng mga IBM device para makakuha ng tumpak na resulta habang binabawasan ang bilang ng shots, oras ng compute, at gastos. <br/><br/>Zero-overhead na paraan na nagpapabuti ng katumpakan ng execution para sa Sampler at Estimator primitives, compatible sa anumang weight ng observable. | S: .5<br/> M: 1<br/>L: 5 |\n"
"| Orbit<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/quantum-elements-orbit)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/quantum-elements-orbit/api-reference) | Quantum Elements | Mga workload na may idle period o scheduling gap, kabilang ang mga static at dynamic na circuit tulad ng quantum error correction, mid-circuit measurement, oracular algorithm, variational quantum algorithm, at Hamiltonian simulation. | Pinagsasama ang optimized na transpilation, dynamical decoupling, at measurement error mitigation sa iisang workflow para mapabuti ang performance ng circuit sa IBM Quantum hardware. <br/><br/>Naglalapat ng low-overhead na error suppression na pinapanatili ang orihinal na lohika ng circuit nang walang karagdagang quantum o classical na pre-processing time, kaya maaaring i-enable, i-disable, o ihambing ng mga user ang bawat teknik sa raw na circuit. | S: 0<br/> M: 1<br/>L: 5 |\n"
"| AI-QEM<br/><br/>[Guide](/guides/ltm-ai-qem)<br/>[API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/functions/ltm-ai-qem/api-reference) | LTM | Mga Estimator workload, lalo na ang mga utility-scale na circuit na may malaking depth at width, tulad ng Hamiltonian simulation at mirror o Clifford benchmarking circuit. | Gumagamit ng graph convolutional network (GCN)-Transformer model, na sinanay sa istruktura ng circuit, topology ng backend, Pauli observable, at qubit calibration, para hulaan ang correction factor para sa bawat Pauli term. <br/><br/>Nililimitahan ang error sa expectation values nang walang karagdagang oras ng QPU kumpara sa Estimator primitive, dahil inilalapat ang correction sa post-processing. | N/A |\n"

